{{!--
    Site navigation: one flat list of links, in the header, the drawer and the
    footer.

    There is deliberately no dropdown. Ghost's navigation is a flat list, so
    nesting has to be faked with a labelling convention — and a convention a
    publisher has to be told about, in a menu that is five items long, buys
    complexity nobody asked for. A header that fits on one line does not need
    submenus.

    Items whose label begins with "- " are skipped rather than shown. That
    marker was the old nesting convention; anyone upgrading with it still in
    their navigation gets those items dropped instead of literal dashes on the
    page.

    {{this.url}}, not {{url}}: Ghost registers `url` as a helper, and a helper
    beats a context property of the same name — {{url}} inside this loop returns
    the *current page's* URL, so every item would link to the same place, with
    nothing in the logs to say so.

    Parameters
      variant   header | drawer | footer
      type      primary (default) | secondary
      label     accessible name for the <nav> landmark
--}}
<nav class="ghost-nav ghost-nav--{{variant}}" aria-label="{{label}}">
    <ul class="ghost-nav__list">
        {{#match type "secondary"}}
            {{#foreach @site.secondary_navigation}}
                <li class="ghost-nav__item">
                    <a class="ghost-nav__link{{link_class for=this.url activeClass=" ghost-nav__link--current"}}" href="{{this.url}}">{{label}}</a>
                </li>
            {{/foreach}}
        {{else}}
            {{#foreach @site.navigation}}
                {{#match label "~^" "- "}}{{else}}
                    <li class="ghost-nav__item">
                        <a class="ghost-nav__link{{link_class for=this.url activeClass=" ghost-nav__link--current"}}" href="{{this.url}}">
                            <span class="ghost-nav__icon">{{> "nav-icon"}}</span>
                            {{label}}
                        </a>
                    </li>
                {{/match}}
            {{/foreach}}
        {{/match}}
    </ul>
</nav>
